ccpatch is an independent open-source project. It is not affiliated
with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Anthropic, PBC.

ccpatch distributes no Anthropic source code. The framework operates
exclusively on a copy of the Claude Code CLI that the user has already
installed on their own machine (typically via `npm install -g
@anthropic-ai/claude-code` or by downloading an official release).
ccpatch reads that user-owned copy, applies declarative patches to it,
and writes the result back to a path the user controls.

"Anthropic", "Claude", and "Claude Code" are trademarks of Anthropic,
PBC. Use of those names in this project is nominative — to identify the
upstream software that ccpatch transforms — and does not imply any
endorsement or affiliation.

The user is solely responsible for ensuring that their use of ccpatch
and of any patched Claude Code build complies with the applicable
Anthropic terms of service, usage policies, and any other agreements
between the user and Anthropic. Running a patched build may alter
behavior in ways that affect that compliance; review the patches you
enable in ccpatch.yml and consult THREAT_MODEL.md before use.

ccpatch ships no telemetry, performs no network calls from the patcher
itself, and has no auto-update mechanism. See THREAT_MODEL.md for a
per-patch breakdown of what each enabled patch reads, writes, and
sends.
